Phase 6 Task 6.3 (bead VieNeuTTSApp-nqx.8.3) — enrollment and the studio speak
the active engine's cloning contract instead of VieNeu's assumptions.

Delivered:
- Controller: `addVoice` becomes stacked overloads — the original
  `addVoice(str, str, bool)` plus `addVoice(str, str, bool, str)` carrying the
  reference transcript — so an older host keeps working while a Qwen Base
  profile gets the transcript its engine requires. Every enrollment is now
  stamped with the profile it belongs to (`profile`), the `transcript` and the
  `consent` flag, and `removeVoice` stamps the profile too, so a clone stays
  attributable after the user switches engines. `refreshVoices()` also emits
  `profileCatalogChanged`, so the profile-scoped catalogs
  (`profileVoices`/`profileClones`) refresh after an enrollment instead of
  rendering the pre-enrollment list.
- EngineState gains the cloning vocabulary: `supportsCloning`,
  `cloneRequirements` (from the capability table), `requiresTranscript`,
  `supportsReferenceCleanup` (= the profile is not a managed install, i.e. the
  bundled engine that can denoise a reference) and `cloningBlockedReason` /
  `hasCloneRequirement()` for surfaces that must explain why they are off.
- CloningTab: a profile that cannot clone at all (Qwen CustomVoice) shows
  `cloneCapabilityNotice` instead of a consent checkbox and a workspace field
  it could never use; a profile that needs a transcript (Qwen Base) shows
  `cloneTranscriptLabel`/`cloneTranscriptField`/`cloneTranscriptHint` and the
  Enroll action stays disabled until it is filled. The denoise row plus
  `referenceCleanupNote` are hidden where the engine rejects a denoise pass
  (`supportsReferenceCleanup`). The clone list now renders
  `controller.profileClones` — the active profile's own clones — and each row
  names its owner via `clonedVoiceProfile` ("Hồ sơ: %1"), so a clone enrolled
  under another profile is visibly not offered here.
- StudioTab: a re-synthesis whose voice no longer belongs to the active
  profile shows `studioRegenProfileBanner`/`studioRegenProfileLabel` with a
  `studioSwitchToRegenProfileButton` (studioSwitchToRegenProfile()) instead of
  silently rendering with a fallback voice — `regenVoice()` now submits
  `regenVoicePicker.effectiveVoice` and never `controller.defaultVoice`.
- StudioClipRow: each rendered clip states its provenance —
  `studioClipProfile`/`studioClipLanguage`, with a legacy clip labelled
  "VieNeu-TTS (bản cũ)" — so a library rendered across engines is readable.
- VoicePicker: `genderLabel`/`styleLabel` return `token || ""`, silencing the
  "Unable to assign [undefined] to QString" warnings for capability rows that
  carry no gender/style.

